3. OVERVIEW ROBOT ANIMATION

The Digitoid robot in Overview should reflect the current review state.

Use the approved Digitoid Brand & Animation Kit.

Do not redesign the robot.

3.1 Required States

Idle

Normal expression with occasional subtle blinking.

Thinking

Gentle eye animation during analysis.

Working

Subtle animation with a meaningful description of the current activity.

Needs Input

Calm attention expression with a clear action request.

Completed

Brief positive expression when the review successfully completes.

Failed

Neutral robot with a clear error message and supported recovery action.

3.2 Animation Requirements

* Preserve the approved robot silhouette.
* Preserve the white head, navy face, white eyes, and red curved accent.
* Do not distort proportions.
* Avoid exaggerated movement.
* No floating effects.
* No arms or antennas.
* No unnecessary glow.
* No animated sidebar logo.
* Respect reduced-motion preferences.
* Provide static fallbacks.
* Avoid unnecessary animation libraries.
* Connect animation to real workflow state.

Do not simulate completion or progress using arbitrary timers.

3.3 Asset Quality

Some existing animation assets may not perfectly match the approved robot.

Inspect them before integration.

If an animation contains artifacts or changes the robot’s appearance, do not use it.

Use the approved static asset instead.

Do not silently replace the robot with another design.

